        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: “If My Friends Could See Me Now”, Sweet Charity\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Neil Simon, Bob Fosse, Gwen Verdon, Lawrence Leritz\n- Characters: Charity, Vittorio\n\nFacts:\n- “If My Friends Could See Me Now” is a song from the 1966 Broadway musical Sweet Charity.\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music for Sweet Charity, Dorothy Fields wrote the lyrics, and Neil Simon wrote the book.\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed Sweet Charity for Broadway.\n- Gwen Verdon, Bob Fosse’s wife and muse, starred in Sweet Charity alongside Lawrence Leritz.\n- In “If My Friends Could See Me Now,” the character Charity reflects on her marvelous luck while spending time with Vittorio.",
