        "original_id": "a7b5147e-0e98-5974-8e90-31b3d265a6f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\", \"Sweet Charity\"\n- People: Cy Coleman, Dorothy Fields, Gwen Verdon, Vittorio, Shirley MacLaine, Bob Fosse, John McMartin\n- Roles: Charity\n\nFacts:\n- \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\" is a song from the 1966 Broadway musical \"Sweet Charity\".\n- Cy Coleman wrote the music for \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\", and Dorothy Fields wrote its lyrics.\n- In \"Sweet Charity\", the character Charity reflects on her marvelous luck while spending time with Vittorio.\n- Gwen Verdon played Charity in the original New York cast of \"Sweet Charity\".\n- Bob Fosse directed and choreographed \"Sweet Charity\" for Broadway.\n- Gwen Verdon and John McMartin starred in the Broadway production of \"Sweet Charity\".\n- In the 1969 film adaptation of \"Sweet Charity\", Shirley MacLaine performed \"If My Friends Could See Me Now\".",
